==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[File:Fat man.jpg|thumb|An early-generation atomic gravity bomb.]]
[[File:Nagasakibomb.jpg|thumb|A mushroom cloud characteristic of an atomic bomb detonation.]]

===Etymology===
Coined by British science fiction author {{w|H. G. Wells}} in his 1914 novel ''{{w|The World Set Free}}''.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|countable|military}} A [[nuclear weapon]] that [[obtain]]s its [[destructive]] [[energy]] from [[nuclear fission]].
#* {{quote-book
|en
|year=1914
|first=Herbert George
|last=Wells
|authorlink=H. G. Wells
|title=The World Set Free
|passage=The gaunt face hardened to grimness, and with both hands the bomb-thrower lifted the big '''atomic bomb''' from the box and steadied it against the side.
}}
#: {{syn|en|atom bomb|A-bomb|fission bomb}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable|colloquial|with '''the'''}} The [[possession]] of one or more atomic bombs; the [[ability]] to [[launch]] a [[nuclear]] [[attack]].
#: {{ux|en|Nine different countries have '''the atomic bomb''' as of 2022.}}
#: {{syn|en|the bomb}}

